cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use, test, extend, or discuss this work, please cite it as below."

title: "Adaptive Representation Processing: An Open Architecture Hypothesis for Runtime Selection of Mathematical Execution Regimes"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Zachary"
    given-names: "David"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Davidsakry/adaptive-representation-processing"

abstract: >
  Adaptive Representation Processing is an exploratory computer-architecture
  hypothesis investigating whether a processing system can dynamically select
  among general, structured/sparse, and relational/geometric execution regimes
  according to observed workload behavior. The project includes transparent
  executable models, fair-baseline comparisons, break-even analysis, and
  explicit falsification criteria. Current results are normalized model
  outputs and are not hardware performance measurements.

keywords:
  - computer architecture
  - adaptive computing
  - reconfigurable computing
  - accelerator architecture
  - sparse computing
  - complex arithmetic
  - runtime adaptation
  - performance monitoring
  - relational processing
  - geometric processing

